{
  "contract": "native-schema-slices.md revision 6",
  "slice": "2d",
  "setup": {
    "notes": [
      "clone cases use the raw fork-like clone (no new stack, SIGCHLD); each child exits immediately with _exit(0) and the parent reaps it",
      "clone.parent_and_child_tid sets CLONE_PARENT_SETTID|CLONE_CHILD_SETTID; clone.pidfd sets CLONE_PIDFD with the parent_tid slot as the pidfd output; clone.clear_child_tid sets CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID",
      "clone3 passes an 88-byte clone_args (CLONE_ARGS_SIZE_VER2) with CLONE_PIDFD|CLONE_PARENT_SETTID|CLONE_CHILD_SETTID|CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID and exit_signal SIGCHLD",
      "semctl cases use a private 3-semaphore set: SETALL {1,2,3} then GETALL, then IPC_RMID; setall_bad_id uses semid -1 (EINVAL before any copy)",
      "process_vm cases target the probe's own PID: readv copies a 16-byte 'ANTINOMIE-REMOTE' buffer into a local one; writev copies 'ANTINOMIE-WRITEV' into another buffer of the probe",
      "set_tid_address runs in child F, which then exits; set_robust_list registers a local empty list head (next points to itself, futex_offset 0) after saving glibc's head with get_robust_list, then restores glibc's head; bad_len passes 16"
    ]
  },
